# 15. Message queue in a Spring Boot application

Since you're learning **Java backend + Spring Boot**, eventually you'll see something like:

```text
Spring Boot
    │
    ▼
RabbitMQ / Kafka
    │
    ▼
Another Spring Boot service
```

For example:

```text
Order Service
Spring Boot
     │
     │ OrderCreatedEvent
     ▼
 RabbitMQ
     │
     ▼
Notification Service
Spring Boot
```

The Spring ecosystem provides integrations such as:

```text
Spring AMQP  → RabbitMQ
Spring Kafka → Kafka
```

So MQ becomes another layer of your backend architecture:

```text
              ┌──────────────┐
              │   Frontend   │
              └──────┬───────┘
                     │ HTTP
                     ▼
              ┌──────────────┐
              │ Spring Boot  │
              │   Service    │
              └──────┬───────┘
                     │
                     │ message
                     ▼
              ┌──────────────┐
              │ Message      │
              │ Broker       │
              └──────┬───────┘
                     │
             ┌───────┴────────┐
             ▼                ▼
        Email Service    Inventory Service
```

